WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.367
-Guys, today is Friday,

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.534
and that's usually when I catch
up on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.400
I check my inbox,
return some emails,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.200
and of course,
I send out thank you notes.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.601
And I was just
running a bit behind.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:09.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Do you guys mind -- James,

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.634
can I get some thank you note
writing music, please?

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:16.534
♪♪

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:17.667
-"M3gan."
-Yeah.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.567
No, it's not "M3gan."

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.634
♪♪

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:27.467
Thank you, Dry January,
for being the month

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.834
where people go a whole week
without drinking.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:32.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.567
-"What's the date?"
-"It's close enough."

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.100
♪♪

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.234
Thank you, Kevin McCarthy.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.400
You know what they say,
if at first you don't succeed,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.067
try, try, try, try,
try, try, try...

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:49.634
and try and try again.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.567
And try and try.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.334
♪♪

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.701
Thank you, Speaker of the House,

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:05.367
for sounding like a fancy name
for your Alexa.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.868
[ Applause ]
"That's the speaker of --"

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.868
My kids changed the Alexa name
the other day.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.067
-What is it?

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.400
-It was like Zippy
or something.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.367
[ Laughter ]
It's terrible. It's a nightmare.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.834
'Cause I go, "Why is
this not working?"

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.167
They go,
"We don't know anything."

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.968
But I guess you could
change the name.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.167
So, I had to find out --
-So you have to go --

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.567
Did you have to say --
-"Zippy, can you change

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.367
your name back to Alexa?"

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:30.834
-But you had to know Zippy.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.367
-Someone had to figure out
Zippy, yeah.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.334
-Hey, man,
it's February 1st somewhere.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.334
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.567
-Thank you, George Santos,

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.634
for being the Pinocchio
of politics.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.801
♪♪

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:53.033
Thank you, Southwest Airlines,
for making people on Spirit

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.501
feel like they just got upgraded
to first class.

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:00.200
♪♪

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.601
-♪ Up in the sky
with my champagne ♪

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.267
[ Air horns ]

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:06.868
♪♪

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:09.067
[ Deep voice ]
Spirit Airlines.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.834
♪♪

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.601
-Thank you, ski lifts,

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:15.801
for not updating your safety
requirements since 1936.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.567
"Pull the pipe down.
Or don't."

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:21.968
-"Grab that rope."

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:24.000
-"Pull the pipe down, or don't.
We don't care."

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.467
♪♪

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.200
Thank you, tiny jugs
of maple syrup,

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.534
for looking like accessories

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.634
for an American Girl doll
moonshine kit.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:36.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.534
"You wanna try some of this?"

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:40.968
-"Yeah, the revolution's
coming."

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.067
-"Oh, this'll put hair
on your chest."

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.767
"You got it, pappy."

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.634
♪♪

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:52.567
-Thank you, "Avatar" sequel,
for being the only movie

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.601
where the positive
and negative reviews

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.567
both say, "It blue."

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.501
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.434
-Come on.

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.200
♪♪

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.767
-Thank you, adding a heart
or a "ha ha" in a text message,

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.100
for being the nicest way to say,

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.033
"I want this conversation
to be over."

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:17.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.467
"Ha ha."

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.968
♪♪

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.567
Thank you, Christmas trees
after the holidays,

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.501
for taking Dry January
way too far.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.667
There you go, everybody.
Those are our thank you notes.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:32.067
We'll be right back with
Allison Williams, everybody.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:33.467
Come on back.

